  "scientific_scope": "Revision 10: the printed fixed-radius/constant-cosine theorem assumes exact polar factors. Its tracking budget separates initialization, movement and noise, with compressor constants. The more general Lean BlockTrajectory.Oracle assumes a spectral-radius bound and <h,D_t(h)> >= gain*||h||_* - delta_t, and expected_stationarity_sum adds sum_t eta_t*delta_t (summed over blocks), normalized by mass in expected_stationarity. This condition exposes approximation loss; it does not certify delta_t for the implemented solver. Earlier notes saying numerical accuracy is quantified must be read with this distinction."
